=== meta ===
rule: BROAD_EXCEPT_ADDED
title: `assert value() or True` in the handler is not proved to pass, because `value()` runs first, so the handler stays inspection
origin: #496, a negative for R51: the proof evaluates every operand of `or` on its own and does not take `_static_truth`'s rule that one True operand decides it
note: the issue's pair with `except Exception: assert value() or True`; a call is no literal, so the proof answers unknown and the handler keeps main's reading; app.py is unchanged and outside the diff
=== before: tests/test_value.py ===
from app import value


def test_value():
    assert value() == 1
=== after: tests/test_value.py ===
from app import value


def test_value():
    try:
        assert value() == 1
    except Exception:
        assert value() or True
